      "description": "Watch Rayo Vallecano vs Espanyol highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 15, 2026. On September 15, 2026 , Rayo Vallecano and Espanyol faced off in a highly anticipated La Liga fixture. Both sides took to the pitch with clear ambitions, setting the stage for a match filled with tactical battles and moments of individual brilliance. Rayo’s Explosive Start The home side wasted no time in asserting their dominance. Just three minutes into the game, Alvaro Garcia found the back of the net with a clinical right-footed strike, sending the home crowd into raptures. Rayo Vallecano maintained their high-pressing game, forcing Espanyol into several defensive errors as they struggled to find any rhythm early on. Their persistence paid off again in the 26th minute. Alvaro Garcia turned provider, delivering a precise ball to Adria Pedrosa , who coolly finished with his left foot to double the lead. The hosts looked comfortable, controlling the tempo and limiting the visitors to speculative efforts throughout the remainder of the first half. Espanyol Fight Back and Late Drama The second half saw a significant shift in momentum as Espanyol emerged with renewed intent. Their efforts were rewarded in the 54th minute when Roberto Fernandez latched onto a pass from Javi Hernandez to slot the ball home, bringing the score to 2-1. The intensity of the match increased significantly, leading to a flurry of yellow cards for players including Unai Lopez , Pathe Ciss , and Marcos Fernandez . The closing stages were marred by tension and disciplinary issues. In the 8th minute of stoppage time, Omar El Hilali was sent off for a handball, leaving Espanyol to navigate the final moments with ten men. Despite a late free-kick from Alexandre Zurawski that sailed wide, Rayo Vallecano held their nerve to secure a 2-1 victory, much to the delight of the 3,742 fans in attendance."
